1. kā́ya, a. relating to the god Ka 🞄(Prajāpati);
 m. nuptial form of Prajāpati;
 🞄root of the little finger (sacred to Prajāpati).

2. kāya, m. body;
 mass, extent, group;
 🞄capital: -kleśa, m. bodily distress;
 -daṇḍa, 🞄m. perfect control over the body;
 -māna, n. 🞄[] 🞄tent of grass, foliage, &c.: i-ka-niketana, n. 🞄id.;
 -vat, a. incarnate;
 -śiro-grīva, n. body, 🞄head, & neck;
 -stha, m. writer (mixed caste).
